module

public import Theory.Representation.AlternatingSevenConjugatePair.SourceLineGeometry.Displacements

/-!
# Distinguished-line geometry of the binary S₇ conjugate pair

For a nonzero vector fixed by the marked Sylow two-subgroup, its stabilizer
is exactly the syntheme overgroup. The cubic and duad residuals move its line
in two-dimensional planes contained in the indicated swap-displacement
commutators with the elementary group generated by the three disjoint swaps.
The syntheme residual fixes the line. These calculations hold for every
supplied conjugate pair, without a model-equivalence hypothesis.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith 14.4.11, printed p.1011/PDF p.1028.
-/
